---
title: "Collections and indexes"
description: "Create and alter dense, sparse, hybrid, multivector, and custom-sharded Qdrant collections."
sidebar:
  order: 5
---

## Collection topology

{% qqlExample title="Dense, sparse, and multivector schema" %}
CREATE COLLECTION research (
  dense VECTOR(384, COSINE),
  bm25 SPARSE,
  colbert VECTOR(128, COSINE)
    WITH MULTIVECTOR (comparator = 'max_sim')
    WITH HNSW (m = 0)
) WITH HNSW (m = 16, ef_construct = 100);
{% /qqlExample %}

Vector names are application-defined. Names such as `dense`, `bm25`, and
`colbert` are conventions, not reserved words. The schema—not the name—defines
the vector role.

## Payload indexes

{% qqlExample title="Filter indexes" %}
CREATE INDEX ON COLLECTION research FOR tenant_id
TYPE keyword WITH (is_tenant = true, on_disk = true);

CREATE INDEX ON COLLECTION research FOR content
TYPE text WITH (
  tokenizer = 'multilingual',
  lowercase = true,
  phrase_matching = true
);
{% /qqlExample %}

Create indexes for fields used frequently in filters or ordering.

## Custom shard keys

{% qqlExample title="Partition management" %}
CREATE SHARD KEY 'acme' ON COLLECTION research
WITH (shards_number = 2);

SHOW SHARD KEYS ON COLLECTION research;

DROP SHARD KEY 'acme' ON COLLECTION research;
{% /qqlExample %}

Shard-key DDL is a remote Qdrant capability and is not supported by the edge
backend.
